{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124121","id":4723444385,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGYoKoQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124121","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124121.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124121.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124121","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124121/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124121/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124121/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/bb6ddb65d61c1333336ed24f91ce782cb2de8ba7","number":124121,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Ensure scaling for remain time decrement is applied after update frame","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123572\r\n- Supersedes/Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123667\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis fix ensure to retrieve the frame speed which is considered when decrementing the remaining time after the frame has been updated. It separates `frame_speed_scale` from the `speed` variable and multiplies only that scale later. Since `speed` is used solely for handling exceptions and determining the direction of progress, and `frame_duration` is guaranteed to be `>= 0.01`, this separation does not affect the existing behavior.\r\n\r\nAlso unify the direction-dependent calculation of `frame_progress`. `abs()` was actually meaningless and forced a sign inversion when calculating `frame_progress`. Removing `abs()` has unified and simplified the calculation.\r\n\r\nThis fix will change the timeline of existing behavior and SpriteAnimation with non-uniform frame times, but it is difficult to see the difference in cases that only include common scaling factors such as x2 or x0.5, so I think this not to be a breaking change.\r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c7750fdd-555c-446d-bf79-6df062bfe7ff\r\n\r\nAfter fix:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d4a1a5f4-d90f-480b-ba03-ec6b28f69389\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/m